    "done_when": "Done when a new tests/test_a_promotion_releases_waiters_however_spelled.py shows four things with a temporary crew home: A trigger plan#§8 makes a waiter on plan#s8 a candidate, and a trigger plan#s8 makes a waiter on plan#§8 one. A waiter on the project:plan#s8 is a candidate for a same-project trigger plan#§8 . A waiter on another plan's #s8 , or on the same plan in another project, is not a candidate. A candidate whose other wait is still pending stays waiting. Four negative controls: the exact-string comparison makes the first case find no candidate; comparing a qualified ref's whole string makes the second case find none; a key without the plan slug, or without the project, makes the third case a candidate; and moving every candidate to queued without re-deriving its waits makes the fourth case leave waiting. The test files importing reckon.crew.queue_admission or reckon.crew.promotion add no failure against the base revision, run one arm at a time with at most -n 4 . Ruff adds no findings on the staged paths. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT= . Write paths: reckon/crew/queue_admission.py , reckon/crew/promotion.py and the new test.",
